  (layer "F.Cu")
  (descr "generic Universal step-down module land pattern (12-24V -> 5V) socket. Generated from modules.json, confidence=USER-SPECIFIED. Source: user spec 2026-08-01, shrunk 2026-08-13: modules in this class run from about 22 x 18 to 30 x 18 mm, so their pins sit about 18-26 mm apart across and 12-15 mm apart up the board. Pads are 12 x 5 mm on a 24 / 12 mm grid, which covers 12-36 mm across and 7-17 mm up. The first cut was 16 x 10 mm, generous in both directions; the height was insurance against a spread that does not exist, since every module in this class is 18 mm wide, and it cost 640 mm2 of solid back-side copper right where the signals cross to the right-hand headers. 240 mm2 now.")
